            <ArticleTitle>Elevated unmethylated and methylated insulin DNA are unique markers of A+β+ ketosis prone diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-195</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1056-8727(17)31186-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jdiacomp.2017.10.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A+β+ ketosis prone diabetes (KPD) is associated with slowly progressive autoimmune beta cell destruction. Plasma unmethylated and methylated insulin DNA (biomarkers of ongoing beta cell damage and systemic inflammation, respectively) were elevated in A+β+ KPD compared to all other KPD subgroups.</AbstractText>
